{
 "notes": [
  "RUMBLING (scene 3, 0x0163e7 input, 0x015fce draw): the area select, each area's sub-menu, the gates and the contest's details. The rules it enters by (regulation, rentals, rankers) are data/world/rumbling.json; the contest held at a venue is the calendar's (tables/town.json).",
  "layers: the backdrop 0x348, the strip 0x36c and the lower strip 0x349 (0x013902). The frame's RIDING SV plate is the screen's own: sprite 0x367 at (370, 335), layer 0x108, the name 76 right and 8 down (0x06db03 with its last argument 1), sliding in from the right.",
  "areas: each area's day and night pictures (0x1d7160 records [day, night, label, title]) at (71, 115) in the picture frame 0x354, its name strip, its logo and its item on the bar (0x06c530; the lit sprite over the normal one, pulsing while the areas take input). The items slide in from item_from_x over slide_seconds and the bar 0x359 from bar_from_x. Changing area cross-fades the pictures over fade_seconds. A venue with no contest shows CLOSED 0x34b over the noise 0x35e. The last area is EXIT.",
  "area_select: the contest's name, class and fee right-aligned on the info panel 0x352 (0x015c44), and CLEAR 0x34a once won (not for the contests in no_clear_mark).",
  "menu: confirming an open area turns to its sub-menu over turn_seconds (0x014895): the pictures fade, the info slides right by info_slide, the logo moves to title_at and the six items (0x1d7100 sprites at 0x1d7130 places) come in from the left by item_slide, each trailing the last. ENTRY is greyed (#404040) without a ridden Scoobee that meets the regulation or in a rentals-only class, RENTAL where rentals are disallowed (0x0138da). The map 0x387 (0x014af3) builds the area's drawing up a frame every map_frame_seconds, the frame before fading out tinted map_fade_colour, and shows its H marks (0x21c72c).",
  "gates: the gate window 0x37c (0x0150ea) with a label per gate the stage has (0x37d to 0x37f, left edge by count in label_x, label_step apart, the chosen one yellow), the gate markers 0x380 on the map and the ring 0x390 turning round the chosen one (0x013a84). In a ranker's contest the ranker holds a gate that cannot be chosen.",
  "contest_info: the INFORMATION window 0x382 pops open (0x013d07) with the details the schedule's popup also draws (contest_info.hpp).",
  "messages: the notices at message_text_at: fee (not enough New Yen, 0x016d0e), no_robot, regulation, rentals_only, no_rentals (0x0137d6), area_ranker and first_ranker (0x09700f).",
  "character_info: WIRE HEADS DATA (0x015aa2, window 0x39b drawn by 0x013f5a). CHARACTER INFO opens (sys 5) when someone is out in the area today (data/world/rumbling.json roster) or the contest is a ranker's, whom it then shows alone; otherwise it refuses (sys 8). Left and right step through the opponents, wrapping (sounds.browse, sys 3); B goes back (sys 8). The window pops open like CONTEST INFO's, centred as 0x0bd3bd and 0x0bd396 place it: the pilot's name (the pilot record's first name entry, 0x0c7a09), the robot's name (the robot record's), the partner's name (the second name entry, shown only with a pilot), the team (0x05fa42; no_team, the original's own text at 0x17bea0, when it has none or \"None\"), and the bounty in NY with the HUD's number writer; the pilot's and partner's faces (the name entries' sprites) at pilot_face and partner_face; the B BACK hint (0x6ded3 at 241, 374). The help line stays the menu item's. Not ported: the markers on the area map. The original moves each opponent along the stage's enemy paths (ENPT resources 0x697 to 0x699 in b00_shinjuku, b01_shibuya and b02_umihotaru.bin) while the area's map is open: 0x0147ff places each at a random path point (0x0580bd, segment kinds other than 0, 1, 6 and 7) with a 120 s timer; 0x0148cf / 0x043db5 step them at 10 units a second (0x0444f7, 0x059fb0, 0x05a2a9, which picks a random next segment, not of kinds 0, 1 or 7), projected onto the map by 0x04407a with the area's placement at 0x1d6fb0, the one shown in yellow. When a timer runs out and more than one is out (0x01476f), that one leaves (0x045da4 puts it back in its pool) and 20 s later another is drawn (0x045a68, 0x0456b7) at a random battle entry point (0x0447cc, table 0x201598). Confirming a gate (0x0169e5) stores each one's path position in its roster record (0x044277: + 0x74, flag + 0x80), and the battle starts it there (0x0825df) unless the contest's class is 22 or 23; others start at a free random entry point. No armour or other state carries over. A ranker's contest shows the ranker's mark at its gate (0x1d7010). The port does not follow those paths yet. A cleared game also raises the opponents' part levels by its laps (0x0456b7), which only the battle would use. The original's tile wipe into the sub-menu (0x0143bf) is a fade here. routes.battle leads to the interim battle (data/world/rumbling.json battle).",
  "robot_markers and each area's robot_map (0x01492b, 0x04407a, 0x04438d; placement 0x1d6fb0, scale 0x1d70d0, origin 0x17beb8, icons 0x200838 by maker and legs type): the opponents out on the area map, turned the way they face; the one CHARACTER INFO shows is chosen_colour with the ring. The live RUMBLING (data/world/rumbling.json live) gives where they stand. character_info armour is a port addition: the shown opponent's armour as it stands, or down while it is shot down."
 ],
